I keep my mental model of junk items as curse catchers this way:

Pretend curse catchers were shaped like those "dream catchers" you buy
at craft fairs to hang in a bedroom window.

If you were going to sew them to your leather armor to catch curses,
would you sew them all on the left shoulder, not really understanding
how they worked?

No, you'd sew one in back first, to catch the "shot from behind", the
next one in front to catch a curse thrown during confrontations, and if
you got others you'd distribute them around as evenly as possible.

The way to distribute _gem_ curse catchers "around evenly" in NetHack is
to give them individual names, so that they cover more slots, just like
the dream catchers cover more directions of attack.

I find this a perfectly natural thing to do in either case versus
stacking all your defenses to defend only one point.

